17592186251966 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251970 13194139533799 true] [17592186251966 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251971 13194139533799 true] [17592186251966 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533799 true] [17592186251966 1041 "selection" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251966 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251971 13194139533799 true] [17592186251966 1110 #uuid "4c42ceb1-23a1-5acb-8615-0e4d492ed9f8" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251967 1034 "x=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+n\\pi " 13194139533799 true] [17592186251967 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533799 true] [17592186251967 1111 #uuid "fd6a47b0-70f8-5535-91bc-f37d35f31daa" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251968 1034 "x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}+4n\\pi " 13194139533799 true] [17592186251968 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533799 true] [17592186251968 1111 #uuid "9cfca77a-46d9-5a9a-abfd-8f0a756dd206" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251969 1034 "x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi " 13194139533799 true] [17592186251969 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533799 true] [17592186251969 1111 #uuid "0b7254f5-1d63-5878-9cfb-9f334bc87dfd" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251970 1034 "x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi " 13194139533799 true] [17592186251970 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533799 true] [17592186251970 1111 #uuid "3c65af0b-b5f1-5b72-a2b0-90f29d5c40fe" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251971 1034 "x=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+4n\\pi " 13194139533799 true] [17592186251971 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533799 true] [17592186251971 1111 #uuid "93450cc6-63e0-5676-8344-8f81d2d5c438" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251972 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251973 13194139533799 true] [17592186251972 1089 "q-117671" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251972 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533799 true] [17592186251972 1100 "Which of the following expressions gives all of the zeros of the function $f(x)=4\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x+\\pi )?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." 13194139533799 true] [17592186251972 1113 #uuid "7ac30df1-20ef-5dc8-9420-e3dd6c1ddd9d" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251972 1145 "The zeros of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ are given by \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the zeros of $f(x)=4\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x+\\pi ),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(3x+\\pi ).$ This gives\n\n$$\n3x+\\pi =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+\\pi  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ 3x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi -\\pi  \\\\ 3x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the zeros are $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3},$ where $n$ is an integer." 13194139533799 true] [17592186251973 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251974 13194139533799 true] [17592186251973 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251975 13194139533799 true] [17592186251973 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251976 13194139533799 true] [17592186251973 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251977 13194139533799 true] [17592186251973 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251978 13194139533799 true] [17592186251973 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533799 true] [17592186251973 1041 "selection" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251973 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251977 13194139533799 true] [17592186251973 1110 #uuid "60ec4258-e789-553b-ba87-3b0438148bab" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251974 1034 "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251974 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533799 true] [17592186251974 1111 #uuid "7eaad2bb-6739-5a3b-a0f0-ff63413cf5f5" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251975 1034 "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{6}" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251975 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533799 true] [17592186251975 1111 #uuid "bc0ab833-15ec-5a78-b98e-b0a5ebc8cd87" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251976 1034 "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251976 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533799 true] [17592186251976 1111 #uuid "c6fd5faa-3ff6-5d33-80f0-4b28ae9e41a8" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251977 1034 "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251977 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533799 true] [17592186251977 1111 #uuid "f0b05473-bcc5-54a5-b454-e7bc84e3a9d6" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251978 1034 "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251978 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533799 true] [17592186251978 1111 #uuid "fc468c49-1e06-5072-93d6-5eb8051c62ee" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251979 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251980 13194139533799 true] [17592186251979 1089 "q-117698" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251979 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533799 true] [17592186251979 1100 "Which of the following expressions gives all of the vertical asymptotes of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." 13194139533799 true] [17592186251979 1113 #uuid "21c3d7aa-d5c5-5b6d-84ac-78dece1c964e" 13194139533799 true] [17592186251979 1145 "The asymptotes of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ are given by the expression\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the asymptotes of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4x+\\frac{\\pi }{4}),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(4x+\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n4x+\\frac{\\pi }{4}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ 4x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\ 4x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{16}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the expression giving all the vertical asymptotes is $x=\\frac{\\pi }{16}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4},$ where $n$ is an integer." 13194139533799 true] [17592186251980 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251981 13194139533799 true] [17592186251980 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251982 13194139533799 true] [17592186251980 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251983 13194139533799 true] [17592186251980 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251984 131941